# Routing

## Route Definitions

- All routes defined in `AppRouter` class annotated with `@AutoRouterConfig`.
- Use nested routes (`children:`) to group related flows. Avoid flat lists of 100+ routes.
- Protected routes use `guards: [AuthGuard()]`.

## Screen Annotations

Every routable page must have `@RoutePage()`:

```dart
@RoutePage()
class LoginPage extends StatelessWidget { ... }
```

## Navigation

- Use `context.router.push(const ProfileRoute())` for forward navigation.
- Use `context.router.replaceAll([const HomeRoute()])` to clear stack (e.g., after login).
- Use `context.router.maybePop()` to go back safely.
- Pass typed arguments via generated route constructors: `ProfileRoute(userId: '123')`.

## Route Guards

```dart
class AuthGuard extends AutoRouteGuard {
  @override
  void onNavigation(NavigationResolver resolver, StackRouter router) async {
    final token = await getIt<SecureStorageService>().getToken();
    if (token != null) { resolver.next(true); }
    else { router.push(const LoginRoute()); resolver.next(false); }
  }
}
```

## After Changes

Run `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs` to regenerate `app_router.gr.dart`.
